proposals.what:
Under the band: 'Confirm this score · 12 questions · about 15 min'.

The server picks the sitting's most uncertain items, in this order:
- rights tagged guess or unsure;
- hard rights answered in under 40% of the tier's median time;
- answers changed in the last minutes;
- flagged rights;
- sure-and-wrong answers;
- then medium items to fill 12.
It serves a twin of each under test rules (source 'confirm', cfg.parent = sid, feedback at the end).

The result on the report:
- '31 right: 27 solid, 4 not confirmed (M1 Q9, M2 Q3, …)' as a strip, with a new cell overlay (confirmed ✓ / not confirmed ?).
- 'Confirmed band 540–660': scoring re-run with each checked item's outcome averaged with its twin's, and the half-band shrunk by √(44/56), from 70 to 62. 'How this is estimated' explains the method.

Other effects:
- estimate.py counts a confirmation and raises confidence one level ('Medium · one section, confirmed').
- When confidence is Low or Medium, the Results estimate card offers 'Raise confidence: confirm Section #7 · 12 questions'.
- Rights that were not confirmed enter Review as unsure mistakes (R9 kind unsure, owed 1).

In the report dialog, choosing 'Wrong answer key' or 'Two answers are right' runs a check before Send. The server regenerates the question from (template, seed), re-runs the topic's independent solver (satbank audit) and, for multiple choice, tests every option against it.

Within a second the dialog shows the key's derivation from the item's own numbers and why the picked option fails, with two buttons: 'Still send it' and 'That explains it'.

If the check disagrees with the key:
- the dialog reads 'Our check disagrees too. Thanks — this question is withdrawn';
- the attempt is marked disputed (R8), so it leaves mastery and the score and the report re-scores;
- the template is flagged for every learner;
- the student sees the outcome in Your reports.

The check's outcome is stored for the admin view.
